<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela bolivar ends flat after intervention.</title>
<headline>Venezuela bolivar ends flat after intervention.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan bolivar ended flat at 470.50/471.50 per dollar, strengthening from 471.50/472.50 earlier in the day after the central bank sold the U.S. currency, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Morning trade saw the dollar rise on moderate demand, but the central bank pulled it back after intervening in the afternoon,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>-- Silene Ramirez, Caracs newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
